<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96988" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμαργ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>noisily prating,
				loud-tongued</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				447
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				607
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. γλωσσαλγία</span>
			<i>wearisome</i> talkativeness, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				525
			</span></i>:—the forms <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στομάργου</span>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στυμ-</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυμ-</span></b>  are
			cited as vv. ll. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στομάργεω</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στυμάργεω</span> (gen. sg. of pr. n.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στομάργης</span> or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στυμάργης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					2.2.4
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.4.5
			</span></i>) by <i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i> Gloss. and others ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.141
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				142
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αργος</span> perh. taken from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλώσσ-αργος</span>.)</div>
